            <ArticleTitle>Executive Summary: European Heart Rhythm Association Consensus Document on the Management of Supraventricular Arrhythmias: Endorsed by Heart Rhythm Society (HRS), Asia-Pacific Heart Rhythm Society (APHRS), and Sociedad Latinoamericana de Estimulación Cardiaca y Electrofisiologia (SOLAECE).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>210-224</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.15420/aer.2016:5.3.GL1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper is an executive summary of the full European Heart Rhythm Association (EHRA) consensus document on the management of supraventricular arrhythmias, published in Europace. It summarises developments in the field and provides recommendations for patient management, with particular emphasis on new advances since the previous European Society of Cardiology guidelines. The EHRA consensus document is available to read in full at http://europace.oxfordjournals.org.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
